# Security checklist

Before merging behaviour that touches auth, data, or user input:

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens)
- [ ] User input validated (Zod at boundaries)
- [ ] SQL via parameterized Supabase client / migrations — no concatenated SQL in app code
- [ ] XSS: no unsanitized HTML from user content
- [ ] AuthZ enforced in RLS policies, not only in UI
- [ ] Error messages do not leak stack traces or internal ids to end users
- [ ] `.env` / credentials not committed

## Supabase RLS

Every new table with user data needs RLS enabled and policies reviewed. Mirror patterns from existing migrations in this repo.

## On finding issues

Stop and use `security-reviewer` agent. Fix CRITICAL before continuing.

